[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186064281 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e" :question/id #uuid "bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48637" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ at the point where $(\\frac{\\pi }{8},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is given by ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,u=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8},$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is $\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cd275e51-d3ee-5c23-a80e-981590060edc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cd275e51-d3ee-5c23-a80e-981590060edc" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd275e51-d3ee-5c23-a80e-981590060edc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9e164b4d-5b5c-55c9-b47c-f00bb1a5bfc2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-16850524-a400-5f1a-93bb-271f14089db2" "answer-9111cb01-85f7-57f5-863f-e240e866660b" "answer-4bf92b52-0c3d-5dbd-ba42-bfbacd464848" "answer-527c209a-b5e6-511e-8fdd-5aa7990f0dc5" "answer-9e164b4d-5b5c-55c9-b47c-f00bb1a5bfc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16850524-a400-5f1a-93bb-271f14089db2" :answer/id #uuid "16850524-a400-5f1a-93bb-271f14089db2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9111cb01-85f7-57f5-863f-e240e866660b" :answer/id #uuid "9111cb01-85f7-57f5-863f-e240e866660b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bf92b52-0c3d-5dbd-ba42-bfbacd464848" :answer/id #uuid "4bf92b52-0c3d-5dbd-ba42-bfbacd464848" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-527c209a-b5e6-511e-8fdd-5aa7990f0dc5" :answer/id #uuid "527c209a-b5e6-511e-8fdd-5aa7990f0dc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e164b4d-5b5c-55c9-b47c-f00bb1a5bfc2" :answer/id #uuid "9e164b4d-5b5c-55c9-b47c-f00bb1a5bfc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064282 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa" :question/id #uuid "c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-48639" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x)$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{8},1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is given by ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{cot}⁡u,\\,u=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=-{csc}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$, we find \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {(\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =-4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is $-4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-28c3ffce-0cd9-54f4-82ea-bc16d219a2b5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28c3ffce-0cd9-54f4-82ea-bc16d219a2b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "28c3ffce-0cd9-54f4-82ea-bc16d219a2b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8f531ae2-78a6-5fc5-abf6-8198a3c1c06e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f1382101-9cdb-5c96-ab81-524b5e88a48f" "answer-8f531ae2-78a6-5fc5-abf6-8198a3c1c06e" "answer-17d5a806-5dea-589a-8695-8f31e73197dd" "answer-99ed28ff-d2ed-5e0a-b7cc-a3079795073c" "answer-a3a3c79b-fcda-5522-aca0-3501669c47af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1382101-9cdb-5c96-ab81-524b5e88a48f" :answer/id #uuid "f1382101-9cdb-5c96-ab81-524b5e88a48f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f531ae2-78a6-5fc5-abf6-8198a3c1c06e" :answer/id #uuid "8f531ae2-78a6-5fc5-abf6-8198a3c1c06e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17d5a806-5dea-589a-8695-8f31e73197dd" :answer/id #uuid "17d5a806-5dea-589a-8695-8f31e73197dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99ed28ff-d2ed-5e0a-b7cc-a3079795073c" :answer/id #uuid "99ed28ff-d2ed-5e0a-b7cc-a3079795073c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a3a3c79b-fcda-5522-aca0-3501669c47af" :answer/id #uuid "a3a3c79b-fcda-5522-aca0-3501669c47af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064283 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8" :question/id #uuid "6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72159" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)=3{cos}^{2}⁡(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=3{u}^{2},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=6u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =6u\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/id #uuid "6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e" "answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" "answer-b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394" "answer-5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe" "answer-ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e" :answer/id #uuid "9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" :answer/id #uuid "41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394" :answer/id #uuid "b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe" :answer/id #uuid "5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96" :answer/id #uuid "ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186065335 :tutorial/content "The chain rule can be used to differentiate trigonometric functions like \n\n$$\ny = \\sin (2x).\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\sin u, \\qquad u = 2x.\n$$\n\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $u=2x,$ we obtain the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064405 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e" :question/id #uuid "bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e"] ["question-bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48637"] ["question-bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ at the point where $(\\frac{\\pi }{8},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}).$"] ["question-bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e" :question/worked-solution "The slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is given by ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,u=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8},$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is $\\sqrt{2}.$"] ["question-bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-cd275e51-d3ee-5c23-a80e-981590060edc" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd275e51-d3ee-5c23-a80e-981590060edc"] ["answer-16850524-a400-5f1a-93bb-271f14089db2" :answer/id #uuid "16850524-a400-5f1a-93bb-271f14089db2"] ["answer-16850524-a400-5f1a-93bb-271f14089db2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-16850524-a400-5f1a-93bb-271f14089db2" :answer