c9a3e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-cd275e51-d3ee-5c23-a80e-981590060edc"] [17592186064281 :knowledge-point/questions "question-bf906107-b91f-584f-aecf-00f5767c9a3e"] ["question-c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa" :question/id #uuid "c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa"] ["question-c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-48639"] ["question-c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x)$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{8},1).$"] ["question-c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa" :question/worked-solution "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is given by ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{cot}⁡u,\\,u=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=-{csc}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$, we find \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =-2{csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {(\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =-4\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ is $-4.$"] ["question-c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-28c3ffce-0cd9-54f4-82ea-bc16d219a2b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "28c3ffce-0cd9-54f4-82ea-bc16d219a2b5"] ["answer-f1382101-9cdb-5c96-ab81-524b5e88a48f" :answer/id #uuid "f1382101-9cdb-5c96-ab81-524b5e88a48f"] ["answer-f1382101-9cdb-5c96-ab81-524b5e88a48f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f1382101-9cdb-5c96-ab81-524b5