b32fa" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-28c3ffce-0cd9-54f4-82ea-bc16d219a2b5"] [17592186064282 :knowledge-point/questions "question-c28249c8-4208-5ae9-84ae-7ac8fd4b32fa"] ["question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8" :question/id #uuid "6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8"] ["question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72159"] ["question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)=3{cos}^{2}⁡(x).$"] ["question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8" :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=3{u}^{2},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=6u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =6u\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =6(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/id #uuid "6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376"] ["answer-9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e" :answer/id #uuid "9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e"] ["answer-9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e" :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" :answer/id #uuid "41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3"] ["answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3" :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["answer-b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394" :answer/id #uuid "b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394"] ["answer-b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394" :answer/value "-6{sin}^{2}⁡x"] ["answer-5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe" :answer/id #uuid "5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe"] ["answer-5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe" :answer/value "3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x"] ["answer-ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96" :answer/id #uuid "ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96"] ["answer-ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96" :answer/value "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/correct "answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3"] ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/choices "answer-9d0f3c8e-bec6-57b5-9ef0-8772ffacc77e"] ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/choices "answer-41ea738c-82ef-5662-96b0-08a42bfce9c3"] ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/choices "answer-b719f5ce-ce7d-56be-82c0-1a11cf55d394"] ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/choices "answer-5ae7c0aa-770c-59f1-a7fd-ae427da7fdfe"] ["answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376" :answer-field/choices "answer-ae283a92-bba7-5715-83f3-e5b4c20c7b96"] ["question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-6740d621-6083-566b-ab24-16955d513376"] [17592186064283 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6d274447-fb0e-53b3-9855-02a8e3567cd8"] [17592186065335 :tutorial/content "The chain rule can be used to differentiate trigonometric functions like \n\n$$\ny = \\sin (2x).\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\sin u, \\qquad u = 2x.\n$$\n\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $u=2x,$ we obtain the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186064405 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0]] "retractions" [[17592186065335 :tutorial/content "The chain rule can be used to differentiate trigonometric functions like \n\n$$\ny = \\sin (2x).\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that this function can be written as the composite function\n\n$$\ny = \\sin u, \\qquad u = 2x.\n$$\n\nWe can use the chain rule to compute the derivative of this composite function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}u)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}u\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $u=2x,$ we obtain the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{cos}(2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"]]}]